Q: How to make a button that switches between two colours? A: <p>You should never try to find a solution only to how it looks. HTML is all about semantics, which are lacking in the question and the answers so far.</p>
<p>Quality code <strong>separates concerns</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>JavaScript and HTML care about semantics</li>
<li>CSS does the visual formatting.</li>
</ul>
<p>That way, the tabs will be usable with the keyboard as well, or with all kinds of assistive technology. It will also help you hide or reveal the according form with <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes/hidden" rel="nofollow noreferrer">the <code>hidden</code> attribute</a>.</p>
<p>You should never have hard-coded style properties in JavaScript.</p>
<p>The pattern you describe is well established as <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/tabs/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Tabs</a>, and documented.</p>
<p>While there is a lot to take in, this is the bottom line for the question at hand:</p>
<ul>
<li>Use <code>aria-selected</code> as the semantic attribute to mark the selected button.</li>
<li>Use JavaScript to toggle that attribute on button click.</li>
<li>Use <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/Attribute_selectors" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Attribute Selectors in CSS</a>, like <code>button[aria-selected=&quot;true&quot;]</code> to apply the correct colour.</li>
</ul>
<p>The following example uses all the documented ARIA attributes for Tabs.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('#log_in_box button[aria-role="tab"]');

buttons.forEach(b =&gt; b.addEventListener('click', e =&gt; {
  // deselect all buttons
  buttons.forEach(b2 =&gt; b2.setAttribute('aria-selected', "false"));

  // finally select the clicked one
  e.currentTarget.setAttribute('aria-selected', "true");
}));</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>#log_in_box {
  margin-top: 100px;
  text-decoration: none;
  margin-bottom: 100px;
  font-size: 20px;
  font-weight: bold;
}

#log_in_box button {
  margin-top: 30px;
  display: inline-block;
  font-weight: bold;
  font-size: 20px;
  right: 5px;
  position: relative;
  bottom: 85px;
  color: white;
  border: 5px solid #a8661f;
  border-radius: 20px 20px 0 0;
  padding: 10px;
  background-color: #d18029;
}

#log_in_box button[aria-selected="true"] {
  background-color: #a8661f;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div id="log_in_box"&gt;
  &lt;div class="box"&gt;
    &lt;div aria-role="tablist"&gt;
      &lt;button id="btn_login" aria-role="tab" aria-controls="form_login" aria-selected="true"&gt;Log In&lt;/button&gt;
      &lt;button id="btn_signup" aria-role="tab" aria-controls="form_signup" aria-selected="false"&gt;Sign Up&lt;/button&gt;
      &lt;div&gt;

        &lt;div role="tabpanel" id="form_login"&gt;
          &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;label&gt;Username:
        &lt;input type="text" name="username"&gt;
      &lt;/label&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;label&gt;Password:
        &lt;input type="password" name="password"&gt;
      &lt;/label&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div role="tabpanel" id="form_signup" hidden&gt;
          …
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
